---
layout: layouts/project.njk
title: Family member demographic
projectId: home-plushy-demographic
permalink: /projects/home-plushy-demographic/
number: "02"
label: THE HOUSEHOLD CENSUS
intro: "Bear’s den is packed with tenants who help themselves to his food, drinks, and clothes. Naturally, they all need IDs: very, very, very illegal Bear-issued cards that are fake, fake, fake. Every plushie is expected to pitch in with cuddling, snuggling, or whatever skills their card says they have. Slackers may be picked up by ICE (Inspection of Cuddling Effort) and face a Facebook Marketplace listing or a shift guarding the trash trailer. Residents can work around the den or move into your computer as Codex pets. Just be warned: they might smash it."
status: The census is getting started
art: plushies
---
<section class="collection-section resident-section" aria-labelledby="residents-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <h2 id="residents-title">Meet the residents</h2>
      <p class="resident-count">{{ plushieIds.length }} residents in the den.</p>
      <p class="gallery-hint">Take a closer look at an ID, or download both sides as a PDF.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="resident-grid">
    {% for resident in plushieIds %}
    <article class="resident-card" aria-labelledby="resident-{{ resident.slug }}">
      <h3 id="resident-{{ resident.slug }}">{{ resident.name | escape }}</h3>
      <a class="resident-image-link" href="{{ resident.image | escape }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View {{ resident.name | escape }}'s full-size ID front (opens in a new tab)">
        <img src="{{ resident.image | escape }}" alt="{{ resident.imageAlt | escape }}" width="{{ resident.width }}" height="{{ resident.height }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </a>
      <div class="resident-downloads">
        <a class="resident-id-download" href="{{ resident.idCard | escape }}" download="{{ resident.slug }}-id-card.pdf" aria-label="Download ID card (PDF) for {{ resident.name | escape }}">Download ID card (PDF) <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></a>
        {% if resident.petPackage %}
        <a class="resident-pet-download" href="{{ resident.petPackage | escape }}" download aria-label="Download Codex pet package for {{ resident.name | escape }}">Download Codex pet package <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></a>
        {% else %}
        {% set matchingFile = codexPets.byResident[resident.slug] %}
        {% if matchingFile %}
        <a class="resident-pet-release" href="{{ codexPets.releaseBase }}{{ matchingFile }}" aria-label="Download Codex pet ZIP for {{ resident.name | escape }}">Download Codex pet ZIP <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></a>
        {% else %}
        <span class="resident-pet-pending">Codex pet package &mdash; coming soon</span>
        {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
<section id="codex-pet-skins" class="collection-section codex-pet-section" aria-labelledby="codex-pets-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">THE DIGITAL RESIDENTS</p>
      <h2 id="codex-pets-title">Codex pet skins</h2>
      </div>
  </div>
  <div class="pet-install">
    <h3>Bring a pet into Codex</h3>
    <p>Download the pet ZIP from its resident card above or from the link below. In a Codex chat that can access your Downloads folder, attach the ZIP or paste its file path, then paste this prompt.</p>
    <pre id="codex-pet-prompt">Please install this ZIP as a custom pet in ChatGPT Work / Codex. Unzip it into a temporary folder and read pet.json. Use the existing v2 sprite sheet, final/spritesheet-extended.png, with the name and description from pet.json. Validate the sheet and use the supported pet upload flow; don’t regenerate the art or replace any existing pet. If you can’t install it here, tell me exactly which file to upload and where.</pre>
    <button type="button" id="copy-pet-prompt" hidden>Copy install prompt</button>
    <span id="pet-prompt-status" role="status"></span>
    <p class="pet-install-note">These ZIPs are asset bundles, not direct installers. If importing manually, unzip first and use the extended PNG. Use <code>final/spritesheet-v1.png</code> only if the importer specifically asks for a 1536 × 1872 sheet.</p>
  </div>
  {% set extraPets = codexPets.packages | rejectattr("residentSlug") %}
  {% if extraPets.length %}
  <h3>Pets without an ID card</h3>
  <ul class="pet-package-list">
    {% for pet in extraPets %}
    <li id="pet-{{ pet.slug }}">
      <a class="pet-zip-download" href="{{ codexPets.releaseBase }}{{ pet.file }}" aria-label="Download {{ pet.name | escape }} Codex pet ZIP">{{ pet.name | escape }} <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></a>
      <span class="pet-zip-size">ZIP · {{ pet.sizeMB }} MB</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}
</section>
<script src="/assets/copy-pet-prompt.js" defer></script>
{% if collections.plushies.length %}
<section class="collection-section resident-stories" aria-labelledby="resident-stories-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="resident-stories-title">Resident stories</h2></div>
  {% set entries = collections.plushies %}{% include "entry-list.njk" %}
</section>
{% endif %}
